# What the README's `go build -o hello-server .` produces...
/hello-server
# ...and what a bare `go build` produces instead: Go names the binary after
# the module path's last element (`module devcroft-nix-go-sample` in go.mod).
# Both, because the README is a suggestion and the default is one keystroke
# away.
/devcroft-nix-go-sample
# `nix build` output symlink into the nix store.
/result
/result-*
